  mode: 0755\n\n        - name: Clean up temporary directory\n          file:\n            path: "{{ tmp_dir.path }}"\n            state: absent\n\n    - name: Create necessary directories\n      file:\n        path: "{{ item }}"\n        state: directory\n        mode: 0755\n      loop:\n        - /etc/rancher/rke2\n        - /var/lib/rancher/rke2\n        - /var/lib/rancher/rke2/etcd\n        - /var/lib/rancher/rke2/etcd/snapshots\n        - /var/lib/rancher/rke2/etcd/backup\n        - /var/lib/rancher/rke2/etcd/backup/snapshots\n\n    - name: Setup RKE2 service\n      block:\n        - name: Create RKE2 config\n          template:\n            src: rke2.conf.j2\n            dest: /etc/rancher/rke2/rke2.conf\n            mode: 0644\n\n        - name: Create RKE2 systemd service\n          template:\n            src: rke2.service.j2\n            dest: /etc/systemd/system/rke2.service\n            mode: 0644\n\n        - name: Enable and start RKE2 service\n          systemd:\n            name: rke2\n            enabled: yes\n            state: started\n\n    - name: Wait for RKE2 to be ready\n      wait_for:\n        host: 127.0.0.1\n        port: 6443\n        timeout: 300\n\n    - name: Verify RKE2 installation\n      command: rke2 version\n      register: rke2_version_output\n      changed_when: false\n      failed_when: rke2_version_output.rc != 0\n\n    - name: Display RKE2 version\n      debug:\n        msg: "{{ rke2_version_output.stdout }}"\n```\n\nThis playbook assumes you have a `rke2.conf.j2` and `rke2.service.j2` template file for the RKE2 configuration and systemd service, respectively. The playbook also cleans up the temporary directory after installation. Make sure you set the `rke2_version` variable before running this playbook.\n\nIt looks like you\'re trying to install RKE2 on multiple hosts, and you\'re encountering an error related to the `rke2` binary not being found. Let\'s walk through the steps to debug this issue.\n\nThe error\n\nThe error 