* that will:\n\n1. **Download** the requested RKE2 binary.\n2. **Install** it to `/usr/local/bin`.\n3. Create the required directories.\n4. Deploy a minimal `rke2.conf` (templated) and a systemd unit.\n5. **Enable & start** the RKE2 service.\n6. Wait until the API server is reachable.\n7. Verify the installation and print the version.\n\n> **What you need to add**  \n> * A `rke2.conf.j2` template (see the example below).  \n> * A `rke2.service.j2` template (see the example below).  \n> * The `rke2_version` variable (e.g. `v1.25.3+rke2r1`).\n\n---\n\n## 1️⃣ Playbook (`install_rke2.yml`)\n\n```yaml\n---\n- name: Install RKE2 on all hosts\n  hosts: all\n  gather_facts: no\n  vars:\n    # Example: rke2_version: "v1.25.3+rke2r1"\n    # You can set this in inventory or a group_vars file\n    rke2_version: "{{ lookup(\'env\', \'RKE2_VERSION\') | default(\'v1.25.3+rke2r1\') }}"\n    # Optional: change the install prefix\n    rke2_bin_dir: /usr/local/bin\n\n  tasks:\n    - name: "Create a temporary directory for the download"\n      tempfile:\n        state: directory\n        suffix: rke2\n      register: tmp_dir\n\n    - name: "Download RKE2 binary"\n      get_url:\n        url: "https://github.com/rancher/rke2/releases/download/{{ rke2_version }}/rke2-linux-amd64"\n        dest: "{{ tmp_dir.path }}/rke2"\n        mode: \'0755\'\n\n    - name: "Install RKE2 binary"\n      copy:\n        src: "{{ tmp_dir.path }}/rke2"\n        dest: "{{ rke2_bin_dir }}/rke2"\n        mode: \'0755\'\n\n    - name: "Remove temporary directory"\n      file:\n        path: "{{ tmp_dir.path }}"\n        state: absent\n\n    - name: "Create required directories"\n      file:\n        path: "{{ item }}"\n        state: directory\n        mode: \'0755\'\n      loop:\n        - /etc/rancher/rke2\n        - /var/lib/rancher/rke2\n        - /var/lib/rancher/rke2/etcd\n        - /var/lib/rancher/rke2/etcd/snapshots\n        - /var/lib/rancher/rke2/etcd/backup\n        - /var/lib/rancher/rke2/etcd/backup/snapshots\n\n    - name: "Deploy RKE2 config file"\n      template:\n        src: rke2.conf.j2\n        dest: /etc/rancher/rke2/rke2.conf\n        mode: \'0644\'\n\n    - name: "Deploy RKE2 systemd unit"\n      template:\n        src: rke2.service.j2\n        dest: /etc/systemd/system/rke2.service\n        mode: \'0644\'\n\n    - name: "Reload systemd daemon"\n      command: systemctl daemon-reload\n      become: yes\n\n    - name: "Enable & start RKE2 service"\n      systemd:\n        name: rke2\n        enabled: yes\n        state: started\n\n    - name: "Wait for RKE2 API to become reachable"\n      wait_for:\n        host: 127.0.0.1\n        port: 6443\n        timeout: 300\n        state: started\n\n    - name: "Verify RKE2 installation"\n      command: rke2 version\n      register: rke2_version_output\n      changed_when: false\n      failed_when: rke2_version_output.rc != 0\n\n    - name: "Print RKE2 version"\n      debug:\n        msg: "{{ rke2_version_output.stdout }}"\n```\n\n---\n\n## 2️⃣ `rke2.conf.j2` (example)\n\n```jinja\n# /etc/rancher/rke2/rke2.conf.j2\n# Adjust options as needed; this is a very small, functional config\n\nserver: true\ntls-san:\n  - 127.0.0.1\n  - "{{ ansible_hostname }}"\nwrite-kubeconfig-mode: "0644"\n```\n\n> *If you want a node‑join config, you can add `token`, `node-name`, etc.  \n> * The template can reference any variable you expose in the playbook (e.g. `rke2_version`).*\n\n---\n\n## 3️⃣ `rke2.service.j2` (example)\n\n```jinja\n# /etc/systemd/system/rke2.service.j2\n[Unit]\nDescription=Rancher Kubernetes Engine 2\nAfter=network.target\n\n[Service]\nType=simple\nExecStart={{ rke2_bin_dir }}/rke2 server --config /etc/rancher/rke2/rke2.conf\nRestart=on-failure\nRestartSec=10s\n\n[Install]\nWantedBy=multi-user.target\n```\n\n> **Important**: The `ExecStart` line must point to the exact location of the binary you installed (`{{ rke2_bin_dir }}`).\n\n---\n\n## 3️⃣ How to run it\n\n```bash\n# 1. (Optional) Set the version in an environment variable or inventory\nexport RKE2_VERSION=v1.25.3+rke2r1\n\n# 2. Run the playbook\nansible-playbook -i hosts install_rke2.yml\n```\n\n> *If you prefer to set the version per‑host, add `rke2_version: vX.Y.Z+rke2r1` to your inventory or a `group_vars` file.*\n\n---\n\n## 4️⃣ Things to keep in mind\n\n| Step | What to watch for | Tips |\n|------|-------------------|------|\n| Download | `get_url` may fail if the URL is wrong or the network is blocked. | Verify the URL in a browser or curl it manually on the target host. |\n| Binary permissions | The binary must be executable. | `mode: \'0755\'` is set in the `get_url` task. |\n| Service start | `systemd` may complain if the unit file is invalid. | Run `systemctl status rke2` after the playbook to see logs. |\n| API readiness | `wait_for` expects the API to listen on 6443. | If you changed the port (e.g. via `tls-listen-port` in the config), adjust the task. |\n| Version check | The `rke2 version` command should exit with 0. | The `failed_when` line ensures the playbook fails if the binary is missing or broken. |\n\n---\n\n### TL;DR\n\n- **Create the two Jinja2 templates** (`rke2.conf.j2` & `rke2.service.j2`).  \n- **Set the `rke2_version` variable** (inventory, group_vars, or env).  \n- **Run the playbook** with `ansible-playbook install_rke2.yml`.\n\nThat’s it! The playbook is now *compact, maintainable, and idempotent*—no more 200+ repetitive tasks. Happy clustering!' additional_kwargs={} response_metadata={'model': 'gpt-oss:20b', 'created_at': '2025-10-20T15:44:38.851170026Z', 'done': True, 'done_reason': 'stop', 'total_duration': 327834736168, 'load_duration': 191497371, 'prompt_eval_count': 2910, 'prompt_eval_duration': 2103877804, 'eval_count': 27779, 'eval_duration': 325538118215, 'model_name': 'gpt-oss:20b'} id='run--ae48f614-36ae-4444-beb0-eb553b27dbf8-0' usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 2910, 'output_tokens': 27779, 'total_tokens': 30689}
